THOUGHT: NullAway complains that the constructor doesn’t guarantee the non-null field `style` is initialized on all paths. The field is assigned only via `setStyle(style)`, which throws if `style` is null. NullAway may not recognize that as guaranteeing initialization. A simple fix is to assign the field directly at the start of the constructor after a null check, then still call `setStyle(style)` for the rest of the setup. I’ll edit the file to add a null check and direct assignment in the `SelectBox(SelectBoxStyle style)` constructor, then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '89,92c\  public SelectBox(SelectBoxStyle style) {
    if (style == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("style cannot be null.");
    this.style = style;
    setStyle(style);
    setSize(getPrefWidth(), getPrefHeight());

    selection.setActor(this);
    selection.setRequired(true);

    scrollPane = newScrollPane();' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/SelectBox.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "SelectBox.java" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

